WEBVTT

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:16.070
Rein...

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:21.960
You're fired.

00:01:59.590 --> 00:02:03.430
Meeting of Fate

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:09.940
<i>Beast Tamer.</i>

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:13.730
<i>It's a class that is able to communicate</i>

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:15.880
<i>and enter into contracts 
with many kinds of animals...</i>

00:02:15.880 --> 00:02:18.280
<i>Taming their strength as your own.</i>

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:25.290
<i>Beast Tamers aren't well-suited to combat,</i>

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:35.590
<i>but I worked hard to support my 
comrades during our harsh journey,</i>

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:39.900
<i>and my comrades in the 
Hero's party trusted me for it.</i>

00:02:41.630 --> 00:02:43.100
<i>Or... so I thought.</i>

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:51.210
Um, hang on a sec.

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:53.980
This is kind of sudden, 
so I'm not sure I follow...

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:56.250
Wait, is this a prank?

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:59.030
Of course not.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:00.560
Arios...

00:03:01.770 --> 00:03:02.800
Aggath?

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:04.340
Leane?

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:06.540
Mina?

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:10.330
You're... serious about this?

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:13.670
I-I want to know why!

00:03:15.410 --> 00:03:16.460
You want a reason?

00:03:17.110 --> 00:03:19.170
You mean other than the obvious one?

00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:22.100
It's because you're useless!

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:24.600
You don't serve any purpose!

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:26.100
Do you get it now?

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:27.470
You've been holding us back so much,

00:03:27.470 --> 00:03:30.520
you even being around 
is more trouble than its worth!

00:03:31.220 --> 00:03:32.430
I am...?

00:03:32.430 --> 00:03:34.480
You have to have noticed, right?

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:36.940
You never do any damage to our enemies,

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:39.900
and we're constantly having to save you.

00:03:40.510 --> 00:03:43.250
All you really contribute 
is scouting and carriage,

00:03:43.250 --> 00:03:45.160
using the animals that you've tamed.

00:03:45.510 --> 00:03:49.100
Doesn't that sound worthless to you?

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:51.330
It was asking too much of
 him in the first place.

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:51.330
<i>What is this...?</i>

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:53.650
We don't have time for babysitting.

00:03:53.650 --> 00:03:57.740
I was always against letting 
a Beast Tamer join up.

00:03:57.740 --> 00:03:59.580
Don't be like that.

00:03:59.580 --> 00:04:04.870
Worthless as he is, I thought he could 
shine by sharing the same spotlight as me.

00:04:04.870 --> 00:04:07.050
Arios, you are so kind!

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:09.540
Very. The only sin here lies with this man

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:13.890
who has wasted the grace of the Hero, Arios.

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:14.900
<i>This is what my party thought 
of me this whole time?</i>

00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:17.470
I... This can't—

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:18.520
Rein...

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:23.280
Don't lower our opinion of you 
any more than you already have.

00:04:25.370 --> 00:04:28.220
And make sure to leave your gear behind.

00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:30.290
We're the ones who gathered it.

00:04:31.060 --> 00:04:34.510
This means we can finally 
take on the Lost Woods.

00:04:34.510 --> 00:04:36.100
We've waited long enough.

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:36.100
I understand.

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:39.910
This town is big, but there's nothing in it, 
and we've been here for days.

00:04:39.910 --> 00:04:43.080
How long was he going to spend 
on gathering supplies, anyway?

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:46.240
We were mistaken to have even 
the most modest hopes for him.

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:48.220
Let us simply consider this a brief respite.

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:49.660
Good idea!

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:53.930
When you put of it that way, maybe he
 was of some use at the very end.

00:04:52.650 --> 00:04:53.930
<i>In that moment...</i>

00:04:54.590 --> 00:04:58.900
<i>It felt like anything between us 
had come to a permanent end.</i>

00:05:19.820 --> 00:05:22.800
You're weak, like a child.

00:05:23.150 --> 00:05:28.340
You still seem to lack both the bearing 
and the skill required of the Hero's party.

00:05:28.770 --> 00:05:32.180
Are you ever going to be good 
for anything besides running errands?

00:05:33.290 --> 00:05:34.430
So worthless...

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:38.650
No need to be so harsh. 
Rein is trying his best.

00:05:39.240 --> 00:05:41.900
<i>At least, for a Beast Tamer!</i>

00:05:42.530 --> 00:05:45.530
<i>I thought the reason they were so hard on me</i>

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:48.740
<i>was because they had high hopes 
for what I could accomplish.</i>

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:50.300
<i>But...</i>

00:05:50.930 --> 00:05:54.580
<i>Maybe they never cared 
about me in the first place.</i>

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:58.730
But more importantly, what do I do now?

00:05:59.310 --> 00:06:01.610
No goal, no gear, and no coin.

00:06:01.610 --> 00:06:04.530
I'm starting with next to nothing.

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:06.800
Rein!

00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:09.600
Did you finish your job for the Hero?

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:11.250
Uh, actually...

00:06:11.250 --> 00:06:12.940
Do the thing then, come on!

00:06:12.940 --> 00:06:13.850
Please!

00:06:13.850 --> 00:06:15.080
Come on, please!

00:06:15.080 --> 00:06:16.320
Do it! Go on!

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:17.180
Okay!

00:06:20.840 --> 00:06:22.360
So, for today...

00:06:28.990 --> 00:06:29.940
There.

00:06:31.420 --> 00:06:33.440
That's the temporary contract.

00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:35.700
Go on, say hello.

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:39.690
Wow!

00:06:39.690 --> 00:06:40.980
Nice job.

00:06:40.980 --> 00:06:41.750
And thank you.

00:06:44.540 --> 00:06:45.290
Bye-bye!

00:06:45.290 --> 00:06:46.700
See you around!

00:06:49.170 --> 00:06:50.690
There it goes...

00:06:50.690 --> 00:06:54.260
Well, like I told you, 
that contract was only temporary.

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:58.670
They're easy to form, 
but they don't last very long.

00:07:01.290 --> 00:07:03.370
Maybe that was a little hard to understand?

00:07:03.370 --> 00:07:05.570
You really are awesome, Rein!

00:07:05.570 --> 00:07:08.280
I wanna be a Beast Tamer when I grow up!

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:09.200
Me, too!

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:10.560
Me, too!

00:07:09.650 --> 00:07:10.560
Huh...

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:12.740
I thought you said you wanted 
to be a hero before?

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:16.290
I mean, the Hero and his party 
always look annoyed

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:18.690
when commoners like us come up to them!

00:07:18.690 --> 00:07:21.720
Even though they suck up 
to rich folks and nobles...

00:07:21.720 --> 00:07:23.440
It's kind of nasty, right?

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:24.330
And scary.

00:07:24.330 --> 00:07:28.090
I didn't know people thought that way 
about Arios and the party.

00:07:28.090 --> 00:07:32.300
I guess that explains the reception 
I got whenever I went to buy supplies.

00:07:32.690 --> 00:07:34.790
You're different though, Rein!

00:07:34.790 --> 00:07:37.210
You always play with us!

00:07:37.210 --> 00:07:38.270
And you're nice!

00:07:39.850 --> 00:07:42.410
<i>It's gonna be even harder 
to tell them I got fired now.</i>

00:07:42.410 --> 00:07:45.760
So I'm gonna be an adventurer, 
and travel all over!

00:07:45.760 --> 00:07:47.560
And make a fortune overnight!

00:07:47.560 --> 00:07:48.440
A fortune!

00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:51.440
A fortune overnight! A fortune overnight!

00:07:48.730 --> 00:07:50.000
An adventurer...

00:07:53.140 --> 00:07:56.540
<i>Living like a migratory bird on 
the wing, free to live or die as I please.</i>

00:07:57.180 --> 00:08:02.410
<i>Making a living off my skills 
by taking jobs as an adventurer?</i>

00:08:03.550 --> 00:08:06.780
<i>Now that I don't need to worry 
about defeating the Demon King,</i>

00:08:06.780 --> 00:08:08.550
<i>it might be the perfect job for me.</i>

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:10.920
Okay!

00:08:11.860 --> 00:08:14.220
Welcome to the Adventurer's Guild!

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:16.740
I'm Natalie, the receptionist.

00:08:16.740 --> 00:08:19.430
Let's start with an explanation 
of the adventurer's trial.

00:08:19.430 --> 00:08:23.680
Could you tell me a bit more 
about being an adventurer first?

00:08:23.680 --> 00:08:27.360
I hate to admit it, but I actually 
don't know that much.

00:08:28.490 --> 00:08:31.010
<i>Arios and the others 
looked down on adventurers,</i>

00:08:31.010 --> 00:08:33.280
<i>so we didn't interact with them much.</i>

00:08:34.250 --> 00:08:35.940
You're an earnest one, aren't you?

00:08:35.940 --> 00:08:39.360
Most of the applicants don't really 
put too much thought into it...

00:08:39.360 --> 00:08:41.710
Personally, I think you're 
on the right track!

00:08:41.710 --> 00:08:42.970
You really do?

00:08:42.970 --> 00:08:44.580
I really do!

00:08:44.580 --> 00:08:46.880
Let's start at the beginning, then.

00:08:47.210 --> 00:08:52.200
Adventurers, like monsters, 
are assigned ranks from S to F...

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:01.430
...and that's everything.

00:09:01.900 --> 00:09:04.110
Is there anything else 
you had questions about?

00:09:04.110 --> 00:09:05.600
Nope. Thank you.

00:09:05.600 --> 00:09:06.900
I should be good, now.

00:09:07.700 --> 00:09:10.870
In that case, let's move onto 
the matter of the adventurer's trial.

00:09:10.870 --> 00:09:12.730
What's your class?

00:09:13.040 --> 00:09:14.500
Beast Tamer.

00:09:15.120 --> 00:09:16.200
Beast Tamer?!

00:09:16.660 --> 00:09:20.200
Um... will you be okay by yourself?

00:09:20.200 --> 00:09:22.740
It's because you're useless!

00:09:23.480 --> 00:09:25.960
Don't do anything reckless, okay?

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:29.820
Adventurers need to know 
when a job is too much.

00:09:30.580 --> 00:09:32.300
Right. Of course.

00:09:36.670 --> 00:09:39.220
Do you understand why 
the guild requires a trial

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:41.720
in order to be registered as an adventurer?

00:09:42.010 --> 00:09:45.240
Is it because if there were 
a bunch of unskilled adventurers,

00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:47.690
it'd undermine trust in the guild?

00:09:47.690 --> 00:09:50.520
Correct! Well done!

00:09:50.520 --> 00:09:53.860
And without that trust, 
the government would get involved.

00:09:55.340 --> 00:10:00.550
But putting that aside, the details 
of the trial involve slaying ten goblins,

00:10:00.550 --> 00:10:02.890
and collecting 20 medicinal herbs.

00:10:02.890 --> 00:10:07.830
Adventurers take on a variety 
hunting and collection jobs,

00:10:07.830 --> 00:10:12.290
so this is the bare minimum required 
to pass muster with the guild.

00:10:20.110 --> 00:10:21.420
That's ten.

00:10:23.060 --> 00:10:26.290
Thanks for helping me find the goblins.

00:10:29.780 --> 00:10:35.180
I guess even a Beast Tamer can 
handle F-ranked monsters like them.

00:10:35.790 --> 00:10:37.740
I've got the rune stones from the goblins,

00:10:37.740 --> 00:10:41.050
so I just need to gather the herbs 
and head back to the guild...

00:10:41.570 --> 00:10:42.600
A scream?

00:10:42.600 --> 00:10:43.610
It's from further in the forest!

00:10:48.780 --> 00:10:50.140
A Killer Tiger?!

00:10:50.700 --> 00:10:51.610
Oh, no!

00:10:52.510 --> 00:10:54.630
<i>The D-Ranked monster Killer Tiger.</i>

00:10:55.270 --> 00:10:59.090
<i>Even a veteran adventurer could be killed 
by one of these if they weren't careful!</i>

00:11:10.880 --> 00:11:13.540
<i>And of course, I don't stand a chance.</i>

00:11:14.110 --> 00:11:14.980
<i>But...</i>

00:11:15.890 --> 00:11:17.040
<i>It's better this way.</i>

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:19.240
Hey, you!

00:11:19.870 --> 00:11:21.150
Can you move?

00:11:21.150 --> 00:11:22.410
You need to run while you can!

00:11:28.700 --> 00:11:30.700
<i>No monsters to tame.</i>

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:33.250
<i>No weapons to use.</i>

00:11:34.090 --> 00:11:37.820
<i>But I can at least buy her 
enough time to get away...</i>

00:11:40.410 --> 00:11:42.660
Wh-Why are you still there?!

00:11:42.660 --> 00:11:44.590
With the last...

00:11:45.900 --> 00:11:47.840
Of my strength...

00:12:14.090 --> 00:12:17.830
<i>Wow. She took down 
a Killer Tiger in one blow.</i>

00:12:18.600 --> 00:12:20.550
Just who are you?

00:12:26.460 --> 00:12:31.480
<i>There are beings of inexplicable power 
in this world known as ultimate species.</i>

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:35.200
<i>Dragonoids. Fairies. Demigods.</i>

00:12:35.200 --> 00:12:37.620
<i>They all count among the ultimate species.</i>

00:12:37.940 --> 00:12:41.360
<i>But one of them is more rare than the rest.</i>

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:42.280
<i>And that is...</i>

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:48.700
A Cat Spirit?

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:54.540
And... I... am... done.

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:55.510
Hey!

00:12:57.060 --> 00:13:00.060
Hey, are you all right? Were you hurt?

00:13:00.060 --> 00:13:01.160
Say something!

00:13:02.070 --> 00:13:02.960
So...

00:13:02.960 --> 00:13:04.060
So?

00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:08.640
So hungry...

00:13:19.730 --> 00:13:22.440
She's... the real deal?

00:13:23.100 --> 00:13:24.780
<i>Despite being one of the ultimate species,</i>

00:13:24.780 --> 00:13:27.410
<i>the Cat Spirits are said to be 
on the verge of extinction.</i>

00:13:28.000 --> 00:13:32.140
<i>They can't use magic, but they've 
evolved to have athletic abilities</i>

00:13:32.140 --> 00:13:34.410
<i>that make them among 
the ultimate in the world.</i>

00:13:36.960 --> 00:13:38.500
<i>And she really is one?</i>

00:13:40.290 --> 00:13:42.400
Thank you so much! You're a life-saver.

00:13:42.400 --> 00:13:44.820
I thought I was gonna die back there.

00:13:44.820 --> 00:13:47.350
I'm just glad I had some 
traveling rations on me.

00:13:47.350 --> 00:13:49.220
Still, are you sure you're not exaggerating?

00:13:49.220 --> 00:13:50.620
Not at all!

00:13:50.620 --> 00:13:52.810
I've gone days without 
anything to eat or drink.

00:13:53.440 --> 00:13:57.390
I could see my grandparents 
in heaven waving me over.

00:13:57.390 --> 00:14:00.170
<i>She must've been in pretty rough shape.</i>

00:14:00.170 --> 00:14:03.050
That would've been another 
step toward extinction.

00:14:03.050 --> 00:14:04.800
<i>Okay, extremely bad shape!</i>

00:14:04.800 --> 00:14:07.360
Oh, I never introduced myself, did I?

00:14:07.790 --> 00:14:11.560
My name's Kanade! 
As you can see, I'm a Cat Spirit.

00:14:11.560 --> 00:14:12.830
Nice to meet you!

00:14:13.460 --> 00:14:15.160
I'm Rein Shroud.

00:14:15.160 --> 00:14:18.450
I ran into you in the middle 
of my adventurer's trial, miss.

00:14:19.540 --> 00:14:20.800
Wh-What is it?

00:14:20.800 --> 00:14:23.880
I'd rather you call me "Kanade" than "miss."

00:14:27.380 --> 00:14:29.180
Okay, if you call me Rein.

00:14:29.180 --> 00:14:31.010
Okay then, Rein!

00:14:33.090 --> 00:14:35.430
I'm glad you're the one who helped me!

00:14:35.700 --> 00:14:39.490
What were you doing out here 
in the first place, Kanade?

00:14:40.130 --> 00:14:43.680
I mean, it's kind of strange 
to find an endangered Cat Spirit

00:14:43.680 --> 00:14:45.920
in some unremarkable forest...

00:14:46.980 --> 00:14:49.360
I've just been traveling, is all.

00:14:49.710 --> 00:14:54.700
There's not many of us, so we 
live quietly, deep in the mountains...

00:14:55.210 --> 00:14:58.160
But life was kind of boring that way,

00:14:58.620 --> 00:15:01.280
so I went on a journey, 
where I ran into you,

00:15:01.280 --> 00:15:02.630
who saved me!

00:15:03.630 --> 00:15:05.840
Feels kind of like fate!

00:15:06.860 --> 00:15:09.300
Now, tell me about you, Rein!

00:15:14.440 --> 00:15:17.140
Then you were in the Hero's party, Rein?

00:15:17.140 --> 00:15:19.180
Yeah. Only for six months, though.

00:15:20.380 --> 00:15:21.740
<i>This is strange...</i>

00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:26.970
<i>Thinking about it has been so depressing, 
I never told anyone else,</i>

00:15:27.950 --> 00:15:30.400
<i>but I'm telling Kanade everything.</i>

00:15:32.110 --> 00:15:33.740
And that's how it went...

00:15:36.100 --> 00:15:36.910
Kanade?

00:15:37.590 --> 00:15:39.600
That Hero ought to be ashamed!

00:15:39.600 --> 00:15:41.500
I can't believe he kicked you out...

00:15:45.190 --> 00:15:47.920
When you're such a nice person!

00:15:48.580 --> 00:15:50.880
Are you mad on my behalf?

00:15:50.880 --> 00:15:52.280
Of course I am!

00:15:52.280 --> 00:15:55.090
Because Rein, you're... I...

00:16:00.570 --> 00:16:03.710
You're really sweet, Kanade. 
But it's okay now.

00:16:05.100 --> 00:16:07.830
They were right about me being a hindrance,

00:16:07.830 --> 00:16:11.570
and I doubt any good would have come 
from staying in that party.

00:16:12.050 --> 00:16:13.260
Okay.

00:16:14.820 --> 00:16:17.490
If you're not mad, Rein, then I'm not mad.

00:16:17.490 --> 00:16:19.120
Still kinda frustrated though...

00:16:20.330 --> 00:16:21.050
Yeah.

00:16:21.510 --> 00:16:23.710
Thank you, though.

00:16:25.040 --> 00:16:27.230
<i>Oh, no! That was on reflex...</i>

00:16:30.980 --> 00:16:33.930
<i>What a relief. She doesn't seem to mind.</i>

00:16:34.510 --> 00:16:37.550
But I want to make one thing clear.

00:16:37.550 --> 00:16:39.940
You're not useless at all, Rein!

00:16:39.940 --> 00:16:42.110
If anything, you're really strong!

00:16:42.110 --> 00:16:44.140
But I'm just a Beast Tamer.

00:16:44.140 --> 00:16:46.940
And you've got an incredible gift for it!

00:16:46.940 --> 00:16:48.130
The reason being...

00:16:48.130 --> 00:16:51.440
I'm pretty sure you could tame me, Rein.

00:16:53.950 --> 00:16:56.090
How do I put this?

00:16:56.090 --> 00:17:00.800
It's like the second I saw you, 
I felt this buzzing, like electricity!

00:17:00.800 --> 00:17:05.200
I thought that you would be 
able to tame me.

00:17:05.200 --> 00:17:10.940
There are only a handful of people in the 
whole world who can tame Cat Spirits!

00:17:10.940 --> 00:17:13.370
Which means you're really amazing, Rein!

00:17:15.590 --> 00:17:18.150
Me, taming a Cat Spirit?

00:17:18.150 --> 00:17:19.990
I never even considered it before...

00:17:19.990 --> 00:17:21.180
Come on, Rein!

00:17:23.540 --> 00:17:25.600
Try taming me!

00:17:29.040 --> 00:17:31.190
<i>If I could actually tame
an ultimate species...</i>

00:17:31.920 --> 00:17:34.540
<i>It would be an unimaginably big help.</i>

00:17:35.650 --> 00:17:38.640
<i>Nothing like that would ever happen again.</i>

00:17:39.060 --> 00:17:40.760
<i>With an ultimate species...</i>

00:17:42.080 --> 00:17:44.540
Feels kind of like fate!

00:17:44.900 --> 00:17:47.040
<i>Oh... that's right.</i>

00:17:48.160 --> 00:17:50.470
<i>It's not because she's from
 an ultimate species.</i>

00:17:51.440 --> 00:17:55.420
<i>I want to get to know Kanade better.</i>

00:17:55.950 --> 00:17:58.130
Okay. Let's try it.

00:17:59.860 --> 00:18:00.850
Yeah!

00:18:22.610 --> 00:18:24.390
My name is Rein Shroud.

00:18:28.510 --> 00:18:32.350
In establishing this new contract,
 a bond is formed.

00:18:34.030 --> 00:18:37.340
An oath in our hearts, hopes in our souls...

00:18:38.100 --> 00:18:39.700
Your power, in my hand.

00:18:40.650 --> 00:18:43.440
Speak now your name.

00:18:44.100 --> 00:18:48.490
<i>If Kanade gives her name now, 
the contract will be formed.</i>

00:18:48.490 --> 00:18:50.270
<i>Otherwise...</i>

00:18:54.270 --> 00:18:55.380
Kanade.

00:19:11.370 --> 00:19:12.540
Did it work?

00:19:12.870 --> 00:19:15.270
Yep. The contract is sealed.

00:19:15.270 --> 00:19:17.460
Look at the palm of your hand.

00:19:18.260 --> 00:19:20.810
There's some kind of weird pattern!

00:19:20.810 --> 00:19:24.260
It's the symbol of what links us.

00:19:24.920 --> 00:19:27.530
You and I are contracted now, Kanade.

00:19:27.530 --> 00:19:32.410
Really? Then this means you 
and I are bound together, huh!

00:19:32.410 --> 00:19:33.770
That's great!

00:19:33.770 --> 00:19:34.870
Bound together?

00:19:35.570 --> 00:19:37.670
Was I wrong?

00:19:37.670 --> 00:19:39.790
No, you're right.

00:19:40.250 --> 00:19:42.990
It symbolizes our bond, Kanade!

00:19:44.290 --> 00:19:45.060
Yeah!

00:19:47.690 --> 00:19:50.270
It's a pleasure to be 
traveling with you, Rein!

00:19:50.270 --> 00:19:51.620
The feeling is mutual!

00:19:55.390 --> 00:19:56.790
Wha—hey!

00:19:57.390 --> 00:20:01.450
<i>There are the ultimate species, 
with inexplicable power...</i>

00:20:01.760 --> 00:20:05.740
<i>I was a Beast Tamer kicked 
out of the Hero's party,</i>

00:20:05.740 --> 00:20:07.400
<i>bereft of a goal or any comrades...</i>

00:20:07.890 --> 00:20:11.520
<i>And now one of the ultimate 
species is working with me.</i>

00:21:46.820 --> 00:21:49.610
Hey, aren't we going back to town?

00:21:49.610 --> 00:21:52.740
I need to finish my adventurer's trial first.

00:21:53.190 --> 00:21:55.600
I think they should be 
around here somewhere....

00:21:56.010 --> 00:21:57.210
Ah, there we go.

00:21:57.210 --> 00:21:58.410
Rabbits?

00:21:58.410 --> 00:22:01.440
Yep. First, a temporary contract...

00:22:05.460 --> 00:22:07.010
There he goes.

00:22:07.010 --> 00:22:10.030
But, wait, Rein how can you—

00:22:10.030 --> 00:22:11.820
Next, he brings his friends over.

00:22:11.820 --> 00:22:12.810
Friends?!

00:22:15.020 --> 00:22:17.510
I'm in fluffy heaven!

00:22:17.510 --> 00:22:20.730
Then I form temporary 
contracts with all of them.

00:22:25.720 --> 00:22:27.370
Okay, everyone,

00:22:27.370 --> 00:22:30.910
I need you to look for medicinal herbs 
in the area and bring them to me.

00:22:31.520 --> 00:22:33.940
Be careful not to mistake them 
for food and eat them!

00:22:34.720 --> 00:22:36.080
Okay, off you go.

00:22:38.000 --> 00:22:39.520
That ought to do it...

00:22:41.580 --> 00:22:43.020
What's wrong?

00:22:43.020 --> 00:22:44.550
What the heck is going on?!

00:22:44.960 --> 00:22:49.410
You were able to tame so many at once! 
And give them complex commands!

00:22:49.410 --> 00:22:51.730
Is that really so rare?

00:22:51.730 --> 00:22:53.390
You bet it is!

00:22:53.390 --> 00:22:59.190
<b>Normal</b>

00:22:53.790 --> 00:22:59.090
Even with temporary contracts, most Beast 
Tamers can only handle one at a time!

00:22:58.980 --> 00:23:04.110
<b>Weird</b>

00:22:59.090 --> 00:23:02.100
Not to mention, you've tamed me,

00:23:02.100 --> 00:23:04.110
so you shouldn't be able to do any more, Rein!

00:23:04.110 --> 00:23:08.820
I mean, I know I said you were 
an amazing Beast Tamer, but...

00:23:08.820 --> 00:23:11.020
This is supposed to be impossible!

00:23:11.020 --> 00:23:13.320
Huh, you know a lot 
about this stuff, Kanade.

00:23:13.320 --> 00:23:14.630
How is this happening?!

00:23:14.630 --> 00:23:17.730
I've never heard of a Beast Tamer
 doing all this at once!

00:23:17.730 --> 00:23:19.170
I'm not sure what to tell you...

00:23:19.880 --> 00:23:22.940
Back home, everyone can do this sort of thing.

00:23:23.570 --> 00:23:25.960
It's just normal for 
a Beast Tamer, isn't it?

00:23:26.940 --> 00:23:29.240
It's not even kind of normal!

00:23:29.240 --> 00:23:33.040
And you called me inexplicable?!

00:23:35.640 --> 00:23:40.020
Comrades

00:23:36.500 --> 00:23:38.730
Next time: "Comrades."
